{"id":"ENGL290","title":"Introduction to Digital Studies","department":"English","level":"Undergrad","credits":"3","description":"Introductory course in digital studies. Surveys contemporary humanities work in digital technologies, including the web and social media and their historical antecedents. Explores design and making as analytical tools alongside reading and writing. Situates digital media within power and politics and develops critical awareness of how media shape society and ethics. Interdisciplinary approaches to creativity, analysis, and technology. While the course will include hands-on practice, no prior experience of programming, designing, or making required other than a willingness to experiment and play.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201908","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":8,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Andy Yeh"],"removed":false},{"term":"202001","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Brittany Starr"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Andy Yeh"],"removed":false},{"term":"202101","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":1,"instructors":["Kyle Bickoff"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Andy Yeh"],"removed":false},{"term":"202201","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Cameron Mozafari"],"removed":false},{"term":"202208","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":6,"instructors":["Brian Davis"],"removed":false},{"term":"202301","sections":2,"seats":40,"openSeats":6,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Porter Olsen"],"removed":false},{"term":"202308","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Kevin Wisniewski"],"removed":false},{"term":"202401","sections":1,"seats":20,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Mehdy Sedaghat Payam"],"removed":false},{"te